# Memory Vessel: "players may play cards they exiled this way" (CR 305.1): a land from exile uses the turn's one land play, so a second
# is refused (Bot1 plays a Mountain from exile, then another Mountain from exile is refused). The Vessel itself, exiled as a cost and
# not by its effect, can't be cast, and the hand rule still holds (a Mountain in hand can't be played).

